# Model and cost policy

- Implementation, tests, debugging, refactoring, configuration, and documentation edits must be typed by Sonnet 5 or Codex.
- Do not implement with Opus 5. If the active model is Opus and the request requires file edits, delegate those edits to Sonnet subagents and keep the Opus session on planning, splitting, and synthesis.
- Opus 5 is allowed for a requested plan or architecture decision, and for orchestrating the Sonnet agents that carry it out.
- Do not use recursive delegation (a subagent spawning further subagents) or model fallbacks whose cost is unclear. Parallel delegation is fine when the chunks touch different files.
- Do not invoke repository skills or build new orchestration/harness layers. Work from the relevant files and the existing Gradle/npm/Compose checks.
- Do not scan the whole repository repeatedly. Start from the requested project, its related tests, and the API contract only when the public API changes.
- Never make paid external LLM calls without explicit approval of the call count and budget.

